# A clip on the instrumented player, to its end (cavekit-flash.md R8, T-578): Sorenson Spark, 120 rows, 29.7 s at 12 frames a second,
# from the corpus cache (tools/host/flash-video-clips.sh makes the gen-* clips). The player's own reports are the checks:
# the stream's metadata, its time moving, NetStream.Play.Stop with the time at the clip's length, and the dropped frames
# counted to the end (a number of the report for R8's table; the bound is 60 % of the clip's frames, above the worst reading of 2026-11-17).
# The picture is read too: drawn while playing and at the end, and its content rate over ten seconds (the minimum is
# set from the stock browser's reading on the same page, docs/rounds/t578-2026-11-17).
id: flash-video-spark-small
section: Flash
item: A Sorenson Spark video of 120 rows plays to its end in the instrumented player: the stream's time reaches the clip's length, the picture is never blank, the dropped frames are counted
shells: enyo mochi mojo
page: http://192.168.1.245:8077/jihad-flash-instr.html?movie=avm2&vars=video=http://192.168.1.245:8097/video/zelda-spark.flv
kit: cavekit-flash.md R8
wait text video "video t=" 10
expect flash-drawn m yes
expect audio running 10
expect flash-rate m 10 7.7 40
expect flash-drawn m yes
expect audio running 4
wait text vend "Play.Stop" 54
expect number vendtime 27.2 30.2
expect number venddropped 0 212
expect flash-drawn m yes
expect plugin 3 alive
